From: Codex folio backport <codex@local>
Subject: [PATCH] E404 folio G2.4b: Convert workingset_refault() to take a folio

Upstream patch 80/90.  workingset_refault() now takes a struct folio, the
one caller resolves page_folio(), and the two page flags it sets
(PG_active and PG_workingset, both PF_HEAD) are set through the folio
accessors, so the operation is anchored on the head page rather than on
whatever the caller happened to pass.

Divergences from upstream, all deliberate:

  - lru_gen_refault() is still called with &folio->page.  That function
    belongs to the MGLRU series, not to the folio conversion, so it is
    left alone; the head page is both what the caller had and the page
    that owns PG_workingset.

  - The three workingset counters are NOT split by file/anon.  Upstream
    writes WORKINGSET_REFAULT_BASE + file, which comes from the vmstat
    rework that also renumbered these enum entries; E404 has the plain
    WORKINGSET_REFAULT / WORKINGSET_ACTIVATE / WORKINGSET_RESTORE.  They
    are charged with mod_lruvec_state(..., nr) instead of
    inc_lruvec_state(...), so the amount stays expressed in folio
    geometry as upstream intends.

  - There is no page_memcg() call to convert.  E404 takes the memcg out
    of the shadow entry via mem_cgroup_from_id(); upstream reads it from
    the folio, which is why it needed folio_memcg() from patch 38.

  - workingset_age_nonresident() does not exist in the E404 4.19 base, so
    the call the upstream patch converts is simply absent here.

  - The lru_note_cost_page() -> lru_note_cost_folio() rename is dropped.
    The whole lru_note_cost() machinery (per-cpu writeback cost accounting,
    added in 5.16) is absent from E404: zero occurrences in the tree.

  - Upstream also deletes inc_lruvec_state() from vmstat.h because it
    becomes unused there.  In E404 it lives in memcontrol.h and is left
    in place; removing a helper is churn with no benefit, and
    dec_lruvec_state() is still used by the G2.4a writeback path.

E404 has a single caller, mm/filemap.c:add_to_page_cache_lru().  The other
two callers upstream converts (do_swap_page() and __read_swap_cache_async())
do not call workingset_refault() in this tree: get_shadow_from_swap_cache()
does not exist here either.

diff --git a/include/linux/swap.h b/include/linux/swap.h
index eb0d5f1..459a788 100644
--- a/include/linux/swap.h
+++ b/include/linux/swap.h
@@ -324,7 +324,7 @@ static inline swp_entry_t folio_swap_entry(struct folio *folio)
 
 /* linux/mm/workingset.c */
 void *workingset_eviction(struct address_space *mapping, struct page *page);
-void workingset_refault(struct page *page, void *shadow);
+void workingset_refault(struct folio *folio, void *shadow);
 void workingset_activation(struct page *page);
 
 /* Only track the nodes of mappings with shadow entries */
diff --git a/mm/filemap.c b/mm/filemap.c
index de77477..4c9381b 100644
--- a/mm/filemap.c
+++ b/mm/filemap.c
@@ -948,7 +948,7 @@ int add_to_page_cache_lru(struct page *page, struct address_space *mapping,
 		 */
 		WARN_ON_ONCE(PageActive(page));
 		if (!(gfp_mask & __GFP_WRITE) && shadow)
-			workingset_refault(page, shadow);
+			workingset_refault(page_folio(page), shadow);
 		lru_cache_add(page);
 	}
 	return ret;
diff --git a/mm/workingset.c b/mm/workingset.c
index 47a9ed8..62219db 100644
--- a/mm/workingset.c
+++ b/mm/workingset.c
@@ -343,14 +343,14 @@ void *workingset_eviction(struct address_space *mapping, struct page *page)
 }
 
 /**
- * workingset_refault - evaluate the refault of a previously evicted page
- * @page: the freshly allocated replacement page
- * @shadow: shadow entry of the evicted page
+ * workingset_refault - evaluate the refault of a previously evicted folio
+ * @folio: the freshly allocated replacement folio
+ * @shadow: shadow entry of the evicted folio
  *
  * Calculates and evaluates the refault distance of the previously
- * evicted page in the context of the node it was allocated in.
+ * evicted folio in the context of the node it was allocated in.
  */
-void workingset_refault(struct page *page, void *shadow)
+void workingset_refault(struct folio *folio, void *shadow)
 {
 	unsigned long refault_distance;
 	struct pglist_data *pgdat;
@@ -361,22 +361,32 @@ void workingset_refault(struct page *page, void *shadow)
 	unsigned long refault;
 	bool workingset;
 	int memcgid;
+	int nr;
 
+	/*
+	 * MGLRU's own refault path stays page-based: lru_gen_refault() belongs
+	 * to the MGLRU series, not to the folio conversion, and it is not
+	 * rewritten here.  Passing &folio->page hands it the head page, which
+	 * is where PG_workingset lives (PF_HEAD), so this is the same page
+	 * the caller had and the right one for the flag.
+	 */
 	if (lru_gen_enabled()) {
-		lru_gen_refault(page, shadow);
+		lru_gen_refault(&folio->page, shadow);
 		return;
 	}
 
+	nr = folio_nr_pages(folio);
+
 	unpack_shadow(shadow, &memcgid, &pgdat, &eviction, &workingset);
 	eviction <<= bucket_order;
 
 	rcu_read_lock();
 	/*
 	 * Look up the memcg associated with the stored ID. It might
-	 * have been deleted since the page's eviction.
+	 * have been deleted since the folio's eviction.
 	 *
 	 * Note that in rare events the ID could have been recycled
-	 * for a new cgroup that refaults a shared page. This is
+	 * for a new cgroup that refaults a shared folio. This is
 	 * impossible to tell from the available data. However, this
 	 * should be a rare and limited disturbance, and activations
 	 * are always speculative anyway. Ultimately, it's the aging
@@ -412,7 +422,15 @@ void workingset_refault(struct page *page, void *shadow)
 	 */
 	refault_distance = (refault - eviction) & EVICTION_MASK;
 
-	inc_lruvec_state(lruvec, WORKINGSET_REFAULT);
+	/*
+	 * Upstream splits these three counters by file/anon
+	 * (WORKINGSET_REFAULT_BASE + file) and charges folio_nr_pages() to
+	 * them.  E404 has the unsplit counters and its memcg comes from the
+	 * shadow entry, not from the folio, so there is no page_memcg() here
+	 * to convert.  The delta form is used so the charge stays expressed in
+	 * folio geometry, as upstream intends.
+	 */
+	mod_lruvec_state(lruvec, WORKINGSET_REFAULT, nr);
 
 	/*
 	 * Compare the distance to the existing workingset size. We
@@ -422,14 +440,14 @@ void workingset_refault(struct page *page, void *shadow)
 	if (refault_distance > active_file)
 		goto out;
 
-	SetPageActive(page);
+	folio_set_active(folio);
 	atomic_long_inc(&lruvec->inactive_age);
-	inc_lruvec_state(lruvec, WORKINGSET_ACTIVATE);
+	mod_lruvec_state(lruvec, WORKINGSET_ACTIVATE, nr);
 
-	/* Page was active prior to eviction */
+	/* Folio was active prior to eviction */
 	if (workingset) {
-		SetPageWorkingset(page);
-		inc_lruvec_state(lruvec, WORKINGSET_RESTORE);
+		folio_set_workingset(folio);
+		mod_lruvec_state(lruvec, WORKINGSET_RESTORE, nr);
 	}
 out:
 	rcu_read_unlock();
